== 6.8 Chapter 6 Practice Drill — 30 Questions

30 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 33 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [In a food chain, the arrow points],
  [at the decomposers],
  [from the food to the feeder],
  [from the feeder to the food],
  [at the sun]
)

#mcq(2, [A food chain always begins with],
  [a carnivore],
  [a herbivore],
  [a producer],
  [a decomposer]
)

#mcq(3, [The second trophic level is occupied by],
  [decomposers],
  [secondary consumers],
  [producers],
  [primary consumers]
)

#mcq(4, [Organisms that break down dead matter are],
  [primary consumers],
  [producers],
  [tertiary consumers],
  [decomposers]
)

#mcq(5, [Only about 10 % of the energy at one trophic level passes to the next because],
  [energy is destroyed at night],
  [animals do not eat much],
  [energy is lost as heat, movement and waste],
  [plants use all the energy]
)

#mcq(6, [A pyramid of energy never inverts because],
  [consumers are always larger],
  [energy increases at each level],
  [energy is lost at each transfer],
  [producers are the smallest]
)

#mcq(7, [A pyramid of numbers can invert when],
  [there are no consumers],
  [energy is lost],
  [one producer supports many consumers],
  [the producers are very large]
)

#mcq(8, [The total mass of living material at each trophic level forms a pyramid of],
  [energy],
  [numbers],
  [biomass],
  [productivity]
)

#mcq(9, [Mutualism is a relationship in which],
  [one benefits and one is harmed],
  [both species benefit],
  [one benefits and one is unaffected],
  [both are harmed]
)

#mcq(10, [The relationship between a remora fish and a shark is],
  [commensalism],
  [mutualism],
  [parasitism],
  [predation]
)

#mcq(11, [A tapeworm in the gut of a mammal is an example of],
  [commensalism],
  [parasitism],
  [competition],
  [mutualism]
)

#mcq(12, [*Rhizobium* in the root nodules of a legume shows],
  [commensalism],
  [mutualism],
  [predation],
  [parasitism]
)

#mcq(13, [The sign convention (+, +) describes],
  [mutualism],
  [parasitism],
  [competition],
  [commensalism]
)

#mcq(14, [Competition between two species is written],
  [(−, −)],
  [(+, 0)],
  [(+, +)],
  [(+, −)]
)

#mcq(15, [A food web is more stable than a food chain because],
  [it has more producers],
  [a consumer can switch to another prey],
  [energy is not lost],
  [it has fewer species]
)

#mcq(16, [Predator and prey populations peak out of step because],
  [prey stop breeding],
  [predators do not eat much],
  [they are the same species],
  [the predator needs time to convert food into offspring]
)

#mcq(17, [Biological control introduces],
  [a new crop],
  [a chemical pesticide],
  [a natural enemy of the pest],
  [a fertiliser]
)

#mcq(18, [One risk of biological control is that the introduced organism may],
  [attack non-target species],
  [improve the crop],
  [die immediately],
  [become a producer]
)

#mcq(19, [Energy leaves an ecosystem mainly as],
  [light],
  [heat],
  [chemical energy],
  [sound]
)

#mcq(20, [Which statement about matter in an ecosystem is correct?],
  [Matter is lost as heat],
  [Matter is recycled],
  [Matter is created by decomposers],
  [Matter flows one way only]
)

#mcq(21, [A herbivore belongs to the],
  [fourth trophic level],
  [second trophic level],
  [third trophic level],
  [first trophic level]
)

#mcq(22, [Two species of finch eating the same seeds in the same tree are],
  [competitors],
  [predators],
  [mutualists],
  [commensals]
)

#mcq(23, [Decomposers are shown outside the food chain because they],
  [eat only plants],
  [are producers],
  [are not living],
  [feed on every trophic level at once]
)

#mcq(24, [About how much energy reaches the tertiary consumer from 100 000 kJ at the producer level?],
  [1000 kJ],
  [100 kJ],
  [10 000 kJ],
  [10 kJ]
)

#mcq(25, [Which of these is a pyramid of numbers that would invert?],
  [Tree → insects → birds],
  [Grass → cattle],
  [Crop → humans],
  [Plankton → fish]
)

#mcq(26, [A parasite differs from a predator in that a parasite],
  [does not feed on the host],
  [is always larger],
  [usually lives on or in the host without killing it quickly],
  [kills its host at once]
)

#mcq(27, [In commensalism the second organism is],
  [unaffected],
  [harmed],
  [benefited],
  [killed]
)

#mcq(28, [Energy enters a food chain as],
  [kinetic energy],
  [chemical energy in food],
  [heat],
  [light energy]
)

#mcq(29, [An example of parasitism is],
  [a cow eating grass],
  [a bee on a flower],
  [mistletoe on a cocoa tree],
  [an orchid on a branch]
)

#mcq(30, [Which of these would most reduce the stability of a food web?],
  [Adding a species],
  [Increasing plant growth],
  [Removing a species with many links],
  [Adding a decomposer]
)

